✅ Keywords are reserved words in C that have predefined meanings. They are part of the language syntax and cannot be used as identifiers.

=====================
| Common C Keywords |
=====================
_________________________________________________________________
| Keyword    | Purpose                                          |
| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `int`      | Integer data type                                |
| `char`     | Character data type                              |
| `float`    | Floating-point data type                         |
| `double`   | Double precision floating-point                  |
| `void`     | No return value / no type                        |
| `if`       | Conditional statement                            |
| `else`     | Alternative condition                            |
| `switch`   | Multiple-choice selection                        |
| `case`     | A branch inside `switch`                         |
| `default`  | Default branch in `switch`                       |
| `for`      | Loop                                             |
| `while`    | Loop                                             |
| `do`       | Do-while loop                                    |
| `break`    | Exit loop or switch                              |
| `continue` | Skip current loop iteration                      |
| `return`   | Return a value from a function                   |
| `const`    | Constant variable                                |
| `sizeof`   | Returns size of data type or variable            |
| `struct`   | Structure declaration                            |
| `union`    | Union declaration                                |
| `enum`     | Enumeration                                      |
| `typedef`  | Create a new type name                           |
| `static`   | Static storage duration                          |
| `extern`   | External variable declaration                    |
| `register` | Suggest register storage                         |
| `volatile` | Prevent compiler optimization                    |
| `goto`     | Jump to a labeled statement                      |
| `signed`   | Signed data type                                 |
| `unsigned` | Unsigned data type                               |
| `long`     | Long integer type                                |
| `short`    | Short integer type                               |
| `auto`     | Automatic local variable (default storage class) |
-----------------------------------------------------------------

✅ Modern C standards add a few more keywords (such as _Bool, _Complex, _Imaginary, and newer standard-specific keywords). 
   The list above covers the keywords you'll use most often while learning C.

Rules for Keywords
-------------------
✅ Keywords have fixed meanings.
✅ Keywords cannot be used as variable names.
✅ Keywords are case-sensitive.

Summary
-------
👉 Keywords are reserved words with predefined meanings in C.
👉 They are part of the C language syntax.
👉 Keywords cannot be used as identifiers (variable names, function names, etc.).
👉 C keywords are case-sensitive.
👉 Examples of keywords include int, char, if, else, for, while, and return.

